---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Moving Cost Calculator — Relocation Cost" description="Build a relocation budget from 
move distance, home size, move type, and additional relocation costs. Free planning estimate for any US 
state-to-state move.">
 <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 pb-28 lg:pb-14">
 <div class="max-w-3xl">
 <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-600">Relocation Cost Suite</p>
 <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Build your moving budget</h1>
 <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">Start with a transport planning estimate, then 
add the costs that can make a relocation more expensive than the move itself.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr]">
 <form id="calculator" class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8" 
novalidate>
 <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Move details</h2>
 <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">From State
 <select id="fromState" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" 
aria-describedby="stateHelp"></select>
 </label>
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">To State
 <select id="toState" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" aria-describedby="stateHelp"></select>
 </label>
 </div>
 <p id="stateHelp" class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">State distance uses great-circle
distance between state centroids as a planning starting point. You can edit the miles manually 
below.</p>
 <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Distance <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(miles)</span>
 <input id="distance" type="number" min="1" max="30000" value="1317" inputmode="numeric" 
aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3 outline-none focus:border-sky-500" />
 </label>
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Home size
 <select id="size" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3">
 <option value="1">Studio / 1 room</option><option value="1.35">2–3 rooms</option><option 
value="1.8">4–5 rooms</option><option value="2.4">6+ rooms</option>
 </select>
 </label>
 </div>
 <label class="mt-5 block text-sm font-semibold">Move type
 <select id="type" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3">
 <option value="0.65">DIY</option><option value="1">Rental truck + labor</option><option 
value="1.65">Full-service movers</option>
 </select>
<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 13 / 27>
 </label>
 <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold">Other relocation costs</h2>
 <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Enter amounts you already know. Leave unknown items at 
zero.</p>
 <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Travel <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="travel" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Temporary housing <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="housing" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Deposits / setup <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="setup" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
 <label class="block text-sm font-semibold">Packing / extras <span class="font-normal text-slate-500">(USD)</span><input id="extras" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="0" aria-describedby="inputError" class="mt-2 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-4 py-3" /></label>
 </div>
 <p id="inputError" class="mt-4 min-h-5 text-sm font-medium text-red-700" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-500">The estimate updates as you type.</p>
 <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
 <button id="share" class="rounded-xl bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-800" type="button">Share this estimate</button>
 <button id="reset" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-50" type="button">Reset calculator</button>
 </div>
 <p id="shareStatus" class="mt-3 min-h-5 break-all text-sm text-slate-500" 
aria-live="polite"></p>
 <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">This calculator covers the planning inputs 
shown above. It does not automatically include taxes, insurance, utility connection fees, or real-estate
costs unless you enter them under “Other relocation costs”. See the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700
underline" href="/methodology">methodology</a> for how the estimate is built.</p>
 </form>
 <aside class="h-fit rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 p-7 text-white sm:p-8 lg:sticky lg:top-6">
 <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Estimated relocation budget</p>
 <div id="result" class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold">$0</div>
 <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">Planning estimate, not a quote. Replace 
assumptions with provider quotes as you get them.</p>
 <div class="mt-7 space-y-3 border-t border-slate-800 pt-5 text-sm">
 <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Move</span><strong 
id="moveResult">$0</strong></div>
 <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Other costs</span><strong 
id="otherResult">$0</strong></div>
 <div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-slate-400">Contingency (10%)</span><strong
id="contingencyResult">$0</strong></div>
 </div>
 <div class="mt-6 border-t border-slate-800 pt-5 text-sm text-slate-400">Indicative range <strong
id="range" class="text-white">$0–$0</strong></div>
 <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900 p-4 text-sm">
 <p class="font-semibold text-slate-200">Published truck-rental average</p>
 <p class="mt-1 text-slate-400">U-Haul published one-way rental average for this mileage band: 
<strong id="marketBenchmark" class="text-white">$0</strong>.</p>
 <p id="floorNote" class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-sky-300" hidden>The move cost starts from
this average because the basic model came out lower.</p>
 <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">It is used only as a minimum base for the 
move cost. It is a mileage-band average, not your route quote.</p>
 </div>
 </aside>
 </div>
 <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-6 text-sm leading-7 text-amber-950">
 <strong>About this estimate:</strong> this MVP uses a transparent planning model, not live mover 
quotes or a market-validated price database. Treat the result as a budgeting starting point and replace 
assumptions with real quotes.
 </div>
 <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="methodology-heading">
 <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-600">How it works</p>
 <h2 id="methodology-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Transparent 
calculation methodology</h2>
<PARSED TEXT FOR PAGE: 14 / 27>
 <div class="mt-5 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
 <div>
 <h3 class="font-semibold">1. State distance</h3>
 <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Selecting two states fills the distance with 
a great-circle calculation between their centroids. This is a planning approximation rather than road 
mileage.</p>
 </div>
 <div>
 <h3 class="font-semibold">2. Known extra costs</h3>
 <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Travel, temporary housing, deposits/setup, 
and packing/extras are added exactly as you enter them. Unknown items remain at zero until you have an 
amount.</p>
 </div>
 <div>
 <h3 class="font-semibold">3. Planning buffer</h3>
 <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">A 10% contingency is added to the move and 
known extra costs. The displayed range is a planning band, not a confidence interval or provider 
quote.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class="mt-6 border-t border-slate-200 pt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
 <p><strong class="text-slate-900">Source notes:</strong> the one-way truck-rental average by 
mileage band comes from <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" 
href="https://www.uhaul.com/Tips/Loading/How-To-Save-Money-ON-Truck-Rentals-35820/" rel="noopener">U-Haul</a> (September 2025 data). It sets the minimum base for the move cost. A BLS labor-wage figure is 
stored for reference and does not change the result.</p>
 <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-slate-900">Current model status:</strong> the DIY base is 
the larger of a simple distance model and the U-Haul average for the mileage band. Rental-truck and 
full-service types add a labor/service premium on top of that base, and that premium is still an 
explicit MVP assumption. Because the U-Haul figures are band averages, the estimate can step up when the
distance crosses a band boundary (for example at 1,000 miles). U-Haul notes that one-way rates vary by 
origin, destination, truck size, move date, and inventory. Validate the result against route-specific 
provider quotes.</p>
 </div>
 </section>
 </section>
 <div class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-20 border-t border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 text-white 
lg:hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite">
 <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center justify-between gap-4">
 <div>
 <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Estimated budget</p>
 <p id="mobileTotal" class="text-xl font-bold leading-6">$0</p>
 </div>
 <p class="text-right text-xs leading-5 text-slate-400">Range<br /><span id="mobileRange" 
class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">$0–$0</span></p>
 </div>
 </div>
 <script src="../scripts/calculator.js"></script>
</Layout>
